# The app's direct dependencies — the file a person edits.
#
# Every one is pinned exactly, to the version production ran on 9/28/26
# (Python 3.12.7, .python-version). Ten of them were ranges: a variable
# change that rebuilt an unchanged commit could pull a new SDK minor, and a
# rollback did not restore the old dependency set (#112 — production had
# already broken once on an anthropic minor; ai_utils.create_with_retry).
#
# requirements.txt is the LOCK generated from this file: every package,
# transitive ones included, pinned. Railway (Nixpacks) and CI install the
# lock, never this file. To change a version, edit it here, regenerate the
# lock (the command is in its header) and let CI's lockfile check prove it.
#
# 9/29/26 security bumps (pip-audit): cryptography 48.0.0 -> 50.0.1, pypdf 5.9.0 ->
# 6.19.0, pillow 12.2.0 -> 12.3.0 — resolved with only those three upgraded
# (every other pin held); the app uses Fernet, PdfReader page text and
# Image/ImageOps, all unchanged across these versions.
